===Etymology 1===
{{PIE word|en|h₂éd}}{{root|en|ine-pro|*weyd-}}
The {{glossary|verb}} is an {{aphetic form|en|atwite|t=(''obsolete'') to blame, reproach|nocap=1}},<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=v|id=1165072605|date=September 2023|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|alt=twit{{sup|2}}|pos=v}}</ref> from {{inh|en|enm|atwiten|t=to attribute (something) to someone; to blame (something) on someone; to accuse or charge (someone) with something; to speak ill of; to taunt}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=atwīten|pos=v|id=MED2966}}</ref> from {{inh|en|ang|ætwītan|t=to blame, reproach; to censure, upbraid; to taunt}}, from {{m|ang|æt-|pos={{glossary|prefix}} meaning ‘at, near; toward’}} + {{m|ang|wītan|t=to accuse; to blame, reproach}} (from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*wītaną|t=to punish; to torment; to know; to see}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*weyd-|t=to see}}).

The {{glossary|noun}} is probably derived from the verb, although it is attested in print earlier.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=''n.''{{sup|1}}|noformat=1|id=5654050852|date=July 2023|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|alt=twit{{sup|1}}|pos=n}}</ref>

